~~ Public | Fact checking has often been treated as a one-and-done task: given a social media post, is it true or not? But that is not how we encounter misinformation online. We get a stream of information, and sometimes we, or an AI agent helping us, need to stop the stream and say, "that is not right!" We train an AI to do this by taking inspiration from the online game show Um, Actually, teaching it to identify checkable claims as evidence arrives, search for supporting information, and decide when it has enough evidence to intervene. If it cannot confidently act early, it waits for more context and then performs a full revision, leading to stronger fact-checking and better-timed corrections.
